# /etc/exports on the server: the desktop's home directory lives on the server and is mounted over NFSv4.
# Replace 10.0.0.0/24 with your LAN.
#
# async: the home export was sync at first; on a single SATA SSD under load a small-file CREATE took ~235 ms
# and the desktop stalled. async brought it to ~0.3 ms. Accepted risk: a server crash can lose the last
# seconds of writes (only one desktop writes at a time).
/srv/export/home        10.0.0.0/24(rw,async,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,fsid=0)
# The notes vault is bind-mounted inside the export and stays sync (also written by Syncthing, CouchDB sync, git).
/srv/export/home/notes  10.0.0.0/24(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,nohide,fsid=11)
